<site-header></site-header>

<main class="atmos" data-screen-label="01 home" id="main">
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <div class="home-hero">
      <div class="home-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="num">01</span> Product Strategy &amp; Go-to-Market</div>
          <h1>I helped creators build careers when content was <span class="accent">still just a hobby.</span></h1>
          <p class="positioning">I help media and creator-economy leaders decide what to build next &mdash; and how to turn an audience into a business. Keynotes, workshops, and advisory.</p>
          <p class="lede">I'm Jason Nellis. I was at Hulu when streaming was still a legal gray area, co-founded a company Facebook bought, and ran product where AI meets creator IP. These days I lead innovation at BoltOS and am building Akaeon. The early, unnamed, is-this-even-a-business part is the part I'm good at.</p>
          <div class="ctas">
            <a href="/speaking" class="btn primary">Explore speaking</a>
            <a href="/advisory" class="btn ghost">Explore advisory</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-writing"><a href="/blog">Or read the writing &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="headshot-frame">
          <div class="corner tl">JN · 2026</div>
          <img src="jason-headshot.jpg" alt="Jason Nellis" width="900" height="1200">
          <div class="scan"></div>
          <div class="corner br">● Cannes, FR</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="v">2007</div>
          <div class="l">Building in media since</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="v">3</div>
          <div class="l">Companies co-founded</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat key">
          <div class="v">2019</div>
          <div class="l">Packagd acquired by Meta</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="v">2</div>
          <div class="l">Active ventures &mdash; BoltOS &amp; Akaeon</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- PROOF -->
  <section class="block" id="proof" style="padding-bottom: 0">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <a class="proof-strip" href="/blog/comedy-time-and-the-format-problem-at-hulu/">
        <span class="proof-metric">$400 <span class="pa">&rarr;</span> $4,000<small>monthly revenue &middot; same content</small></span>
        <span class="proof-copy">At Hulu, repackaging an existing comedy library into themed compilations multiplied its monthly revenue tenfold &mdash; same footage, a different format.</span>
        <span class="proof-go">Read the case study &rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WORK WITH ME -->
  <section class="block" id="work-with-me" style="padding-bottom: 0">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="block-head">
        <div>
          <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="num">02</span> Work with me</div>
          <h2>Three ways to put this to work.</h2>
          <p class="block-sub">A keynote, a day with your leadership team, or a longer engagement. Same operator either way.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="offer-grid">
        <a class="card offer-card" href="/speaking">
          <span class="kind">Keynote</span>
          <h3>One argument, forty-five minutes.</h3>
          <p>Built from things I built rather than things I read. For conferences, industry summits, and executive offsites that want a point of view instead of a landscape tour.</p>
          <span class="go">See the talks →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card offer-card" href="/advisory#workshop">
          <span class="kind">Workshop</span>
          <h3>Half a day on one strategic question.</h3>
          <p>Your AI roadmap, your go-to-market, or how you make money from an audience. Your leadership team in the room, a decision on the table by the end of it.</p>
          <span class="go">Ask about a workshop →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card offer-card" href="/advisory">
          <span class="kind">Advisory</span>
          <h3>Ninety days or a monthly retainer.</h3>
          <p>For founders and exec teams deciding what to build and how to explain it. Fixed fee, scoped up front, narrative first. I do the work myself.</p>
          <span class="go">How advisory works →</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="offer-note"><span class="live-pill"><span class="live-dot"></span>MIPCOM · Cannes · 12–15 Oct 2026</span> I'll be on the floor at the Palais des Festivals all week. In town? <a href="/contact">Let's find a table.</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SELECTED WORK -->
  <!-- ls -a -->
  <section class="block" id="work">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <a href="/ascii" class="egg-link" aria-label="hidden">.</a>
      <div class="block-head">
        <div>
          <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="num">03</span> Selected work</div>
          <h2>The career, in three acts.</h2>
          <p class="block-sub">Nearly twenty years of building from the inside — mostly on things that didn't have a category yet.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/jasonnellis" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn ghost">LinkedIn ↗
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-arc">
      <div class="work-connector"></div>
      <div class="work-grid">
        <article class="card work-card act-1">
          <span class="bg-num">01</span>
          <div class="ix"><span class="node"></span>001 / 2007 – 2012</div>
          <div class="era">Learning on the Go</div>
          <h3>Hulu — content &amp; product</h3>
          <p>Started in content partnerships — strategy for accounts from the White House to NBCUniversal — and moved into product and growth as streaming scaled. Learned the distance between a good idea and a product people will actually use, and got a permanent taste for building at scale.</p>
          <div class="meta">
            <span class="role">Content · Product</span>
            <span>Media · Streaming</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="card work-card act-2">
          <span class="bg-num">02</span>
          <div class="ix"><span class="node"></span>002 / 2016 – 2023</div>
          <div class="era">Acquired → Meta</div>
          <h3>Packagd — co-founder</h3>
          <p>Co-founded an influencer monetization startup, acquired by Facebook. Built Facebook Live Shopping in the Commerce org, then moved to NPE to lead Super. Became the team's first Founder in Residence.</p>
          <div class="meta">
            <span class="role">Co-Founder</span>
            <span>Social Commerce · Meta</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="card work-card act-3">
          <span class="bg-num">03</span>
          <div class="ix"><span class="node"></span>003 / 2024 – 2026</div>
          <div class="era">CPO → CEO</div>
          <h3>SuperBam — chief product officer</h3>
          <p>Built the product org from the ground up — creator IP protection, monetization infrastructure, an AI deepfake takedown system. Later stepped into the interim CEO seat.</p>
          <div class="meta">
            <span class="role">CPO / CEO</span>
            <span>Creator Economy · IP</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      </div>
      <p class="block-sub" style="margin-top: 28px">Act four is already underway — leading innovation at BoltOS, building the product infrastructure that turns creator and brand relationships into revenue, and co-founding Akaeon, an early-stage media and events company.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WRITING TEASER -->
  <section class="block" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="block-head">
        <div>
          <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="num">04</span> Recent writing</div>
          <h2>Thinking out loud about the creator economy — usually because something wasn't sitting right.</h2>
        </div>
        <a href="/blog" class="btn ghost">All essays
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="post-list">
        {%- for essay in collections.recentEssays %}
        <a class="post-row" href="{{ essay.url }}">
          <span class="date">{{ essay.data.date | dotDate }}</span>
          <span class="title">{{ essay.data.title }}<span class="read">{{ essay.data.readTime }}</span></span>
          <span class="tag">{{ essay.data.category }}</span>
          <span class="arrow">→</span>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      <!-- NEWSLETTER -->
      <div class="subscribe-banner" style="margin: 48px 0 0">
        <div class="sub-content">
          <span class="sub-eyebrow">Newsletter</span>
          <p class="sub-headline">Get <em>The Long Yes</em> in your inbox.</p>
          <p class="sub-body">Essays on the creator economy and the businesses being built around it &mdash; sent when there's something worth saying, which isn't often.</p>
          <form class="sub-form" action="https://jasonnellis.substack.com/subscribe" method="get" target="_blank">
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="your@email.com" required class="sub-input" autocomplete="email">
            <button type="submit" class="btn primary sub-btn">Subscribe</button>
          </form>
          <p class="sub-note">Powered by Substack &middot; Unsubscribe anytime</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PODCAST -->
  <section class="block" id="podcast" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="podcast-grid">
        <a class="podcast-plate" href="/building-value" aria-label="Building Value — the podcast">
          <img src="building-value-header.jpg" alt="Building Value with Jason Nellis — How creative work becomes a business" width="1672" height="941">
        </a>
        <div class="podcast-copy">
          <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="num">05</span> The podcast</div>
